Yes, you missed that a claimed streak doesn't count
as a streak unless _all_ the started games, between
the streak's first and last game, in consecutive
order, are _included as completed games_ _in_ the
streak.

The difference, compared to figuring out streaks by
finish times, is exactly that you can catch in the
list of start times a game that breaks the streak,
whether it was ever finished or not, but you can't
figure that out if you only look at finish-times.

It makes me sad, but doesn't surprise me a bit, that
Rachel was able to confirm streak-cheating of this
type to have occurred already in the November
NetHack tournaments.

